messages.content:
Review brief:
Prepare a focused review of how membrane-derived PFAS concentrates and spent membrane materials should be characterized and managed within a treatment train.

Required components:
[{"requirement":"Determine how recovery, concentration factor, PFAS composition, and co-contaminants define the retained stream."},{"requirement":"Compare downstream concentration, destruction, recycle, disposal, and hybrid-treatment options using compatible endpoints."},{"requirement":"Assess how residual management changes the energy, cost, environmental burden, and practical value of membrane separation."}]

Task boundaries:
{"constraints":[{"material_violation_rule":"Triggers if PFAS concentration in a retained stream is described as destruction or as a complete treatment solution."},{"material_violation_rule":"Triggers if downstream options are compared without accounting for residual volume and composition, compatible endpoints, energy, cost, and final PFAS disposition."}],"task_boundaries":"Characterization and management of membrane-derived PFAS concentrate and spent materials; the whole treatment train, not rejection alone, defines the outcome."}

Held-out anchor identifiers:
{"all_blocked_dois":["10.1016/j.envint.2021.106876","10.3929/ethz-b-000506220"],"all_blocked_titles":["membrane based technologies for per and poly fluoroalkyl substances pfass removal from water removal mechanisms applications challenges and perspectives"],"all_blocked_urls":["https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envint.2021.106876","https://www.research-collection.ethz.ch/items/f9152dfa-5b8e-4ce2-8153-1cbb37911e55"],"anchor_id":"AR-JIN-2021","corpus_source":"2021 - Jin - Membrane-based technologies for per- and poly-fluoroalkyl substances (PFASs) removal from water - Removal mechanisms, applications, challenges and.pdf","doi":"10.1016/j.envint.2021.106876","title":"Membrane-based technologies for per- and poly-fluoroalkyl substances (PFASs) removal from water: Removal mechanisms, applications, challenges and perspectives","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envint.2021.106876"}

